 Hi Steve!  It seems that I am the KNP guru in these parts (I've created
two games with this thing...one of them is going to be SHAREWARE) so I
think I can answer you questions.

 RANDOM NUMBER GENERATOR: I don't know how it is seeded, sorry.  The
count starts at 0.
 USER INPUT: will take a lot of input, because the program will not
directly read more than one keypress at a time.  You could set up plays
by making a question object, then store a value (for later use) in a
counter object depending on how the user "answered the question".
 VARIABLES: every object has three alterable values (A, B, C) which can
be set at will, and an internal value.  These values carry over from
level to level as long as you 'bring the object over' from another level
via the object shelf arrow buttons.
 
 Hope this helps.  If you have any more questions or need details, just
ask.
 
 Chase


